  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Unlike most cultivars of Acer circift. natum which have shallowly lobed leaves, 'Monroe' has dissected leaves. The five to seven Acer lobes are separated entirely to the base, with Hawthorn the sides of each lobe deeply cut, almost to the An midrib. These sublobes are toothed, forming companion very irregular margins. This sturdy plant forms nials, an upright bush to 13 ft. (4 m) tall, becoming large, broad with age. holds"
